{"version":2,"slug":"repeat-after-me-shadowing-practice-english-pronunciation-training","videoId":"eIYMv9jrGL4","videoUrl":"https://youtu.be/eIYMv9jrGL4","lang":"en","title":"Repeat After Me + Shadowing Practice | English Pronunciation Training","category":"Daily life","channel":"Miss Honey 🍯","channelUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/@Slow_English_Podcast","captionSource":"auto","tags":["English Conversation","learn english"],"backUrl":"/","lines":[{"start":0,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":3,"text":"Let's shadow"},{"start":5,"text":"real life English situations"},{"start":10,"text":"while practicing"},{"start":12,"text":"the words"},{"start":14,"text":"that are difficult to pronounce."},{"start":17,"text":"I asked you guys on Instagram"},{"start":21,"text":"to send me the words you struggle with"},{"start":26,"text":"the most in English."},{"start":28,"text":"So, if you'd like to be a part of the"},{"start":32,"text":"next video"},{"start":34,"text":"then follow me on Instagram. Now,"},{"start":37,"text":"let's start."},{"start":40,"text":"The day I missed my bus"},{"start":44,"text":"in mountain town."},{"start":48,"text":"I woke up"},{"start":50,"text":"at"},{"start":390,"text":"["},{"start":390.6,"text":"in a small"},{"start":391.2,"text":"mountain town."},{"start":391.8,"text":"I looked outside"},{"start":392.4,"text":"and saw an eagle"},{"start":393,"text":"flying above"},{"start":393.6,"text":"the mountains."},{"start":394.2,"text":"The view"},{"start":394.8,"text":"was"},{"start":395.4,"text":"literally"},{"start":396,"text":"incredible."},{"start":396.6,"text":"I thought to myself."},{"start":397.2,"text":"I think"},{"start":397.8,"text":"this"},{"start":398.4,"text":"is one"},{"start":399,"text":"of the coolest places"},{"start":399.6,"text":"in the world."},{"start":400.2,"text":"All right? If you had trouble"},{"start":400.8,"text":"pronouncing think versus"},{"start":401.4,"text":"this,"},{"start":402,"text":"remember,"},{"start":402.6,"text":"think you blow."},{"start":403.2,"text":"And you put your tongue in between"},{"start":403.8,"text":"your teeth."},{"start":404.4,"text":"Think."},{"start":405,"text":"Now for this,"},{"start":405.6,"text":"we blow and vibrate."},{"start":406.2,"text":"The same position of our tongue."},{"start":406.8,"text":"This."},{"start":407.4,"text":"Feel your throat and say"},{"start":408,"text":"think."},{"start":408.6,"text":"No vibration."},{"start":409.2,"text":"Now vibrate."},{"start":409.8,"text":"This."},{"start":410.4,"text":"Perfect. Another good word to practice"},{"start":411,"text":"is"},{"start":411.6,"text":"mountain"},{"start":412.2,"text":"because"},{"start":412.8,"text":"we don't always pronounce"},{"start":413.4,"text":"mountain"},{"start":414,"text":"as mountain."},{"start":414.6,"text":"When we're speaking quickly,"},{"start":415.2,"text":"we can say"},{"start":415.8,"text":"mountain."},{"start":416.4,"text":"Mountain."},{"start":417,"text":"It's like you're cutting out the T."},{"start":417.6,"text":"Mountain."},{"start":418.2,"text":"That's a beautiful mountain over there."},{"start":418.8,"text":"I live in Mountain Town."},{"start":419.4,"text":"Last one."},{"start":420,"text":"Literally."},{"start":420.6,"text":"The T sounds more like a D."},{"start":421.2,"text":"Literally."},{"start":421.8,"text":"And the A is a a."},{"start":422.4,"text":"Literally."},{"start":423,"text":"All right."},{"start":423.6,"text":"Next part."},{"start":424.2,"text":"I walked through the town"},{"start":424.8,"text":"and stopped at a small"},{"start":425.4,"text":"coffee shop."},{"start":426,"text":"The woman"},{"start":426.6,"text":"working there"},{"start":427.2,"text":"smiled"},{"start":427.8,"text":"and said,"},{"start":428.4,"text":"\"Good morning."},{"start":429,"text":"Are you visiting"},{"start":429.6,"text":"these mountains"},{"start":430.2,"text":"for the first time?\""},{"start":430.8,"text":"I said,"},{"start":431.4,"text":"\"Yes."},{"start":432,"text":"I thought"},{"start":432.6,"text":"I would stay"},{"start":433.2,"text":"for two days."},{"start":433.8,"text":"But now"},{"start":434.4,"text":"I think"},{"start":435,"text":"I might stay"},{"start":435.6,"text":"longer.\""},{"start":436.2,"text":"She laughed"},{"start":436.8,"text":"and said,"},{"start":437.4,"text":"\"Those"},{"start":438,"text":"are usually"},{"start":438.6,"text":"the first words"},{"start":439.2,"text":"visitors say."},{"start":439.8,"text":"All right."},{"start":440.4,"text":"Let's practice some words here. visiting"},{"start":441,"text":"visiting sounds like a z"},{"start":441.6,"text":"not an s."},{"start":442.2,"text":"Not visiting."},{"start":442.8,"text":"vi-zi-ting"},{"start":443.4,"text":"Now we have another word there."},{"start":444,"text":"laughed"},{"start":444.6,"text":"Laughed has two things I want to"},{"start":445.2,"text":"mention."},{"start":445.8,"text":"g h in English makes the f sound."},{"start":446.4,"text":"laugh"},{"start":447,"text":"cough"},{"start":447.6,"text":"rough"},{"start":448.2,"text":"tough"},{"start":448.8,"text":"g h"},{"start":449.4,"text":"And in this particular e d ending"},{"start":450,"text":"we pronounce it"},{"start":450.6,"text":"t."},{"start":451.2,"text":"Any ending of a verb"},{"start":451.8,"text":"with the f"},{"start":452.4,"text":"sound"},{"start":453,"text":"sounds like t"},{"start":453.6,"text":"when we add e d."},{"start":454.2,"text":"So, laugh present, laughed"},{"start":454.8,"text":"in the past."},{"start":455.4,"text":"When we add e d, it can either make the"},{"start":456,"text":"t, d, or ed sound."},{"start":456.6,"text":"In this case"},{"start":457.2,"text":"it's t."},{"start":457.8,"text":"And let's practice one more."},{"start":458.4,"text":"visitors"},{"start":459,"text":"vi- zi-"},{"start":459.6,"text":"tors"},{"start":460.2,"text":"visitors"},{"start":460.8,"text":"Not visitors."},{"start":461.4,"text":"visitors"},{"start":462,"text":"Even though it looks like it would sound"},{"start":466,"